The method also checks if the input strings are not null or empty, handles exceptions gracefully, and limits the total length of the concatenated string to 1024 characters. If the combined length exceeds this limit, it truncates the strings proportionally to preserve the integrity of the hash computation.

The code also includes a logging mechanism using java.util.logging library for centralized monitoring and logging. It uses a ConcurrentLinkedQueue to add strings from the external data source, ensuring thread safety under high-concurrency scenarios.

Finally, an interface named Rule is defined which can be used for dynamically adding processing rules for different data types in the future. The current implementation does not include any rule, but you can implement it as needed.']

