[" Here's a basic implementation of the `DataCollector` class in JavaScript. This code doesn't include all edge cases, but it provides a good starting point.

```javascript
class DataCollector {
  constructor(messageInterval, bufferSize, logFunction) {
    this.isRunning = false;
    this.isPaused = false;
    this.buffer = [];
    this.bufferSize = bufferSize;
    this.messageInterval = messageInterval;
    this.timerId = null;
    this.logger = logFunction;
  }

  start() {
    if (this.isRunning) return;

    this.isRunning = true;
    this.timerId = setInterval(() => {
      if (!this.isPaused && this.buffer.length > 0) {
        this.sendDataToMessagingSystem();
      }
    }, this.messageInterval);

    this.logger(`DataCollector started at ${new Date()}`);
  }

  stop() {
    if (!this.isRunning) return;

    clearInterval(this.timerId);
    this.isRunning = false;
    this.timerId = null;

    this.logger(`DataCollector stopped at ${new Date()}`);
  }

  pause() {
    if (!this.isRunning) return;

    this.isPaused = true;
    this.logger(`DataCollector paused at ${new Date()}`);
  }

  resume() {
    if (!this.isRunning || !this.isPaused) return;

    this.isPaused = false;
    this.sendBufferedData();

    this.logger(`DataCollector resumed at ${new Date()}`);
  }

  getState() {
    return { isRunning, isPaused };
  }

  reset() {
    this.buffer = [];
    this.logger(`Buffer reset at ${new Date()}`);
  }

  flush() {
    if (!this.isRunning) return;

    const dataToSend = this.buffer.splice(0, this.buffer.length);
    this.sendDataToMessagingSystem(dataToSend);
  }

  sendDataToMessagingSystem(dataToSend = []) {
    // Implement sending messages to the messaging system here
    // Handle connectivity issues and graceful recovery if necessary
    console.log(`Sending data: ${dataToSend} at ${new Date()}`);
  }
}
```

This implementation includes methods for starting, stopping, pausing, resuming, getting the state of the collector, resetting the buffer, and flushing all buffered data immediately. The class also logs each operation and state change with timestamps.

Remember to implement the `sendDataToMessagingSystem` method according to your messaging system requirements. For handling intermittent connectivity issues, you may consider using a queue for messages or implementing retry logic in the `sendDataToMessagingSystem` method.

Good luck with your project! If you have any questions or need further assistance, feel free to ask."]

