The code does not explicitly handle errors such as failed file reads or memory allocation failures, but you can extend it to do so by checking return values and calling perror() or similar functions for debugging purposes. For better performance under varying load conditions, consider using an appropriate data structure like a linked list or array based on your specific requirements.']

