    char buffer[1024];
    size_t read;

    while ((read = fread(buffer, 1, sizeof(buffer), file)) > 0) {
        // Perform validation on the data before inserting it into the storage.
        if (validate_data(buffer, read)) {
            storage_push(&storage, buffer, sizeof(reading_t));
        }
    }

    fclose(file);

    // Implement your logic for accessing and processing data from the storage here.

    storage_deinit(&storage);
    return 0;
}
```

In this implementation, a custom circular buffer is used to store reading structs, minimizing memory usage while ensuring efficient data retrieval. Concurrent reads and writes are handled using the `pthread_cond_t` variables for synchronization without mutex locks. The trade-off between immediate data insertion and batch processing has been addressed by implementing a loop that continuously reads data from the file.

This function is modular, extensible, and minimally coupled with other components through well-defined APIs. It is designed for future enhancements and can easily be updated to store additional data fields or a larger number of readings without significant code refactoring.']

